In a previous discussion, James inquired about displaying estimates in R alongside their 90% confidence intervals with a clear format. He shared his method of "X [Y - Z]", where X is rounded mean, Y and Z are the lower and upper bounds respectively. I acknowledged that while his approach is clear, a more standard format is "X (95% CI [Y, Z])". I also provided an R function to generate formatted strings based on mu, ci05, and ci95 that dynamically adjusts the number of significant digits based on shared figures between the confidence interval bounds. The function aims to enhance readability while maintaining precision, ultimately offering James a versatile solution for multiple estimates.
